#[doc("""
Kaikai values across the C boundary as `void *` userdata.

`retain_userdata` parks a private copy of a value behind a `Userdata[T]` handle, which an
`extern "C"` import passes to C and an exported `extern "C" fn` receives
back; `take_userdata` reads a fresh copy of the value, `release_userdata` frees the parked one.
The handle keeps the copy alive for as long as C may call back, on any
thread. State belongs in actors: park the `Pid` of the owner and send it
messages from the callback.

All three need `Ffi`. The handle carries the type it was retained at, so a take cannot
read another type; a take or release after a release traps.
""")]

#[doc("A kaikai value of type `t` parked for C; crosses the boundary as `void *`.")]
extern "C" pub opaque Userdata[t]

#[doc("Parks a private copy of `v` and returns its handle.")]
extern "kai"("kai_ffi_retain") pub fn retain_userdata[t](v: t) : Userdata[t] / Ffi

#[doc("A fresh copy of the value parked behind `u`; the handle stays valid.")]
extern "kai"("kai_ffi_take") pub fn take_userdata[t](u: Userdata[t]) : t / Ffi

#[doc("Frees the value parked behind `u`; a later take or release of the handle traps.")]
extern "kai"("kai_ffi_release") pub fn release_userdata[t](u: Userdata[t]) : Unit / Ffi
